From 061c7cf1c2c833db1071bbc189ac116da3c2715f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Profile::GetMesg(num): replace the linear scan with a lazily
 built lookup table

What: the first call builds a 65536-entry static table num -> index; later calls are one array read.
Why it might be faster: GetMesg was a linear scan over all message types, called for every message record. Biggest step in this series (about 6% at search time).
Risk: lazy initialisation uses a plain bool flag, so the first calls from several threads would race. Not tested. Costs 128 KB of static memory.

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 17, region 574 (Profile::GetMesg).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.9369 -> 0.8795 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_17.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_profile.cpp | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_profile.cpp b/src/fit_profile.cpp
index 87c099a..a9973fa 100644
--- a/src/fit_profile.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_profile.cpp
@@ -3057,13 +3057,29 @@ const Profile::MESG Profile::mesgs[MESGS] =
 
 const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
 {
-    for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
+    static FIT_UINT16 lookup[65536];
+    static bool initialized = false;
+
+    if (!initialized)
     {
-        if (mesgs[i].num == num)
-            return &mesgs[i];
+        for (int i = 0; i < 65536; ++i)
+            lookup[i] = 0xFFFF;
+
+        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
+        {
+            const FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
+            if (lookup[n] == 0xFFFF)
+                lookup[n] = static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(i);
+        }
+
+        initialized = true;
     }
 
-    return NULL;
+    const FIT_UINT16 idx = lookup[num];
+    if (idx == 0xFFFF)
+        return NULL;
+
+    return &mesgs[idx];
 }
 
 const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const std::string& name)
